All the working repository is currently on the Jetson. 
To connect via SSH, find out what commands need to be run on your laptop.
In our case, I'm running 22.04.5 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish), and used these commands:

Step 1: Find your laptop's Ethernet interface name
Open your terminal and run:

nmcli device

Step 2: Create the Jetson Network Profile
Run this command to create a permanent network profile that forces your laptop to act as the 192.168.50.1 master.
(Replace <INTERFACE_NAME> with the name you found in Step 1!)

sudo nmcli con add type ethernet con-name "Jetson-Direct" ifname <INTERFACE_NAME> ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses 192.168.50.1/24

Step 3: Wake up the port
Force your laptop to apply the new profile:

sudo nmcli con up "Jetson-Direct"


Step 4: SSH into the Jetson
Now that your laptop is the master, the pipeline is open. Run:

ssh user@192.168.50.2


Running rc jimny instructions:
Connect the main power source coming from the car's battery to the boards and drivers.
Power the jetson.
Connect through ethernet to the jetson with your computer.
Switch ignition on of the Jimny, but don't start the engine yet.
Open four terminals, ssh into the jetson (see here) in each one.

1) put cube-usb cable in the vertical slot of the jetson
2) Put steering-board-usb cable in one of the horizontal usb ports
3) Run this command to check if it is in the correct port (the correct one is USB0 for the steering, otherwise change the commands below to the right port):
  ls /dev/tty*CH* /dev/ttyUSB*
4) Attach the sterfboard-usb cable in the last port
5) 
In terminal 1, 
      cd /workspaces/jimny/jimny_ws
      ros2 run cuberos cuberos_node.py
(expect  "no message received"  message but it's fine)

In terminal 2
      cd /workspaces/jimny/jimny_ws
      ros2 run to_vehicle to_vehicle /dev/ttyCH341USB1

In terminal 3
      cd ~/ackermann_to_steering_serial 
      python3 ackermann_to_steering_serial_final.py /dev/ttyCH341USB0

In terminal 4
      cd /workspaces/jimny/jimny_ws
      ros2 run mode_switching switch


Start the car.
Turn on the Herelink Handheld controller,
Select manual mode
Arm

To power off the jetson via ssh (ALWAYS do this before disconnecting power from the jetson), run this command in one of the ssh terminals:
      sudo poweroff
